{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  OTODOR Module: Lead Form  (Quote / Consultation / Survey capture)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose:            Convert a high-intent visitor into a qualified, attributed
                      lead (quote / site survey / consultation) via the native
                      Shopify `contact` form — plus an instant WhatsApp path.
  Primary source:     Section settings + `reason` / `interest` blocks. A lead
                      form is config-driven, not metafield-driven.
  Fallback order:     interest blocks → single message field only;
                      reason blocks → omit the left trust rail.
  Visibility rule:    Always renders (a contact form is never "empty"), but every
                      sub-part (trust rail, interest select, WhatsApp, consent)
                      self-hides when it has nothing to show.
  Merchant editable:  YES — all copy, fields, interest options, trust reasons,
                      trust-reason style (ledger / icon), colour scheme,
                      WhatsApp toggle.
  Layout register:    Editorial, not carded. The two columns are separated by a
                      single rule (a horizontal one when stacked); the trust
                      reasons are a hairline ledger with a tabular index; the
                      fields are underlines, not boxes; one filled control per
                      action row (WhatsApp is an outline pill carrying the real
                      WhatsApp mark, not a green slab).
  Required metafields: none.
  Optional metafields: none. Reads `product` / `collection` in the render
                       context for hidden lead-attribution fields; uses
                       settings.otodor_whatsapp_number / _enabled / _message.
  Dependencies:       snippets/otodor-icon.liquid; otodor-base.css tokens.
                      Native `{% form 'contact' %}`. Tiny inline script: prefill
                      from ?interest=/?product=/?msg= query params + rebuild the
                      WhatsApp link live from the fields the visitor has typed
                      (name/phone/email/interest/message). Static wa_link is the
                      no-JS fallback.
  Preset:             Full split layout — heading + 3 trust reasons + 4 interest
                      options + phone/email/message + WhatsApp. Renders live.
  Accessibility:      <section aria-labelledby>, <label> per field, aria-required
                      on required fields, error aria-describedby, visible focus,
                      success panel tabindex=-1 autofocus (Dawn parity).
  Reusable for:       Quote page, contact page, PDP footer, collection footer,
                      landing pages, homepage CTA.

  CONTEXT CAPTURE (the native trick): each hidden contact[Label] field arrives
  as a labelled line in the merchant's contact email, so a quote request lands
  pre-attributed (which product / collection / page it came from).
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign scheme = section.settings.color_scheme | default: 'light'
  assign anchor = section.settings.anchor_id | default: 'otodor-lead' | handle
  assign lead_form_id = 'otodor-lead-form-' | append: section.id

  # interest options come from `interest` blocks
  assign interest_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'interest'
  assign reason_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'reason'

  # WhatsApp dual-path
  assign wa_enabled = false
  if section.settings.show_whatsapp and settings.otodor_whatsapp_enabled and settings.otodor_whatsapp_number != blank
    assign wa_enabled = true
    assign wa_number = settings.otodor_whatsapp_number
    assign wa_base = section.settings.whatsapp_message | default: settings.otodor_whatsapp_message | default: 'Hello OTODOR, I would like a quote.'
    assign wa_context = ''
    if product != blank
      assign wa_context = ' — Product: ' | append: product.title
    elsif collection != blank
      assign wa_context = ' — Category: ' | append: collection.title
    endif
    assign wa_intro = wa_base | append: wa_context
    assign wa_text = wa_intro | url_encode
    assign wa_link = 'https://wa.me/' | append: wa_number | append: '?text=' | append: wa_text
  endif
-%}

{%- style -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The wrapper used to carry `otodor-section` as well, which applies
    --otodor-section-py on top of the padding set here: 100px from the class
    plus 96px from the setting = 196px top and bottom. With the neighbouring
    sections' own bands either side, this one form floated in roughly 600px
    of dead space. The class is off the schema now, so this rule is the only
    source of the section's padding.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The setting is the desktop maximum, not a constant: a flat 80px held its
    full height on a phone while every neighbouring section relaxed to ~44px,
    so the form re-opened the gap on exactly the screens with least room.
    Same clamp shape as --otodor-section-py, with the merchant's value as the
    ceiling.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} {
    padding-top: clamp(2.75rem, 6.5vw, {{ section.settings.padding_top | default: 80 }}px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(2.75rem, 6.5vw, {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | default: 80 }}px);
    scroll-margin-top: 90px;
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    Two rule colours, not one: --lead-rule draws structure (the column
    divider, the ledger rows), --lead-line draws the field underlines, which
    have to be a step stronger or a form on a plain background stops reading
    as a form.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    `color-scheme` is what tells the browser which side its native form-control
    defaults sit on. Without it a control's UA text colour resolves to
    `FieldText` — black — so the moment anything knocks out our `color: inherit`
    (autofill, an extension, a stale cached stylesheet) the typed value goes
    black on a black field and the visitor cannot read what they typed. It also
    fixes the parts CSS never reached: the caret, the select's popup, and the
    textarea's scrollbar.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--light {
    color-scheme: light;
    background: var(--otodor-bg-light); color: var(--otodor-ink);
    --lead-accent: var(--otodor-accent-on-light);
    --lead-rule: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
    --lead-line: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22);
    --lead-tint: rgba(26, 120, 216, 0.05);
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--dark {
    color-scheme: dark;
    background: var(--otodor-black); color: var(--otodor-white);
    --lead-accent: var(--otodor-blue);
    --lead-rule: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    --lead-line: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.26);
    --lead-tint: rgba(77, 166, 255, 0.06);
  }

  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__inner {
    max-width: var(--otodor-container);
    margin-inline: auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: clamp(1.75rem, 6vw, 2.5rem); }
    {% if section.settings.form_first %}#otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__aside { order: 2; } #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__panel { order: 1; }{% endif %}
  }

  /* ─ Left rail (value proposition) ─────────────────────────── */
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__eyebrow {
    display: block; font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: 0.96rem; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-widest); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; color: var(--lead-accent);
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__title {
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display);
    /* One section-heading size across the page (was 37.5px against 50px). */
    font-size: var(--otodor-text-4xl); font-weight: 700;
    line-height: var(--otodor-leading-display); letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-tight); margin: 0;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--light .otodor-lead__title { color: var(--otodor-ink); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--dark  .otodor-lead__title { color: var(--otodor-white); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__title .accent { color: var(--lead-accent); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__sub { margin: 1.1rem 0 0; font-size: var(--otodor-text-md); line-height: 1.55; opacity: 0.6; max-width: 34rem; }

  {%- comment -%}
    The trust rail is a ledger, not a card list. Three tinted icon tiles with a
    title and a line under each is the stock "features" component; the same
    three claims read as evidence when they are hairline-ruled rows with a
    tabular index — the register the comparison sheet and the spec table
    already use. `reason_style: icon` keeps the old treatment available, minus
    the tinted plate.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__reasons {
    list-style: none; margin: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3.25rem) 0 0; padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--lead-rule);
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__reason {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.75rem 1fr; align-items: start;
    gap: 0 1.1rem; padding: 1.15rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--lead-rule);
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__reason-index {
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: var(--otodor-text-xs); font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-wider); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--lead-accent); padding-top: 0.32rem;
  }
  {%- comment -%} Icon variant: the glyph only, at rail weight — no plate, no fill. {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__reason-icon {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    width: 2rem; height: 2rem; margin-top: 0.1rem; color: var(--lead-accent); opacity: 0.85;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__reason-icon svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__reason-title {
    display: block; font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--otodor-text-base); letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-base); margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__reason-text { margin: 0; font-size: var(--otodor-text-sm); line-height: 1.5; opacity: 0.55; }

  /* ─ Right column: the form, on the page — not in a box ──────
     It used to sit in a #121212 card on a #0B0B0B section: an edge with
     nothing behind it, a shadow with nothing to cast onto, and a second
     radius inside the first as soon as the inputs were drawn. One rule
     separates the columns instead — the same divider idiom as the rest of
     the site's editorial splits.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__panel {
    padding-left: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--lead-rule);
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    Stacked, the divider belongs above whichever column comes second — so it
    follows the form-first setting rather than being pinned to the form.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__panel { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; }
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__{% if section.settings.form_first %}aside{% else %}panel{% endif %} {
      padding-top: clamp(1.75rem, 5vw, 2.5rem); border-top: 1px solid var(--lead-rule);
    }
    {%- unless section.settings.form_first -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Stacked, the ledger's closing rule and the form's opening rule land
        22px apart — two parallel lines saying one thing. The divider closes
        the ledger and opens the form; the last row gives up its own.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__reason:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    {%- endunless -%}
  }

  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__form { display: grid; gap: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem); }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__field { display: grid; gap: 0.15rem; }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__label {
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: var(--otodor-text-xs); font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-wider); opacity: 0.5;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__label .req { color: var(--lead-accent); opacity: 0.9; }

  {%- comment -%}
    Underlines, not boxes. A boxed field inside a boxed card is two frames
    around one value; the rule under the text is enough to say "type here" and
    lets the type sit on the page at reading size.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__input,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__select,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__textarea {
    width: 100%; font-family: var(--otodor-font-body); font-size: var(--otodor-text-base); color: inherit;
    min-height: var(--otodor-control-h);
    padding: 0.55rem 0; border: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--lead-line);
    border-radius: 0; background: transparent; box-shadow: none;
    transition: border-color var(--otodor-dur-fast) var(--otodor-ease-out),
                background-color var(--otodor-dur-fast) var(--otodor-ease-out);
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    Belt to the color-scheme braces: the colour is stated per scheme rather
    than inherited, and stated twice. `-webkit-text-fill-color` is what
    actually paints the glyphs in a WebKit/Blink form control and it outranks
    `color`, so declaring it here means a UA or extension rule that wins
    `color` still cannot repaint the text.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--dark .otodor-lead__input,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--dark .otodor-lead__select,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--dark .otodor-lead__textarea {
    color: var(--otodor-white); -webkit-text-fill-color: var(--otodor-white);
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--light .otodor-lead__input,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--light .otodor-lead__select,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--light .otodor-lead__textarea {
    color: var(--otodor-ink); -webkit-text-fill-color: var(--otodor-ink);
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    The placeholder has to name its own fill for the same reason — it inherits
    the declared text-fill above, which would print it at full strength.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__input::placeholder,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__textarea::placeholder {
    color: currentColor; -webkit-text-fill-color: currentColor; opacity: 0.35;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__textarea { resize: vertical; min-height: 6.5rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  {%- comment -%}
    Focus is a 2px accent rule (the border plus a 1px shadow under it) and a
    faint wash across the field — a ring can't be drawn round a control that
    has no box. Both are non-colour-only: the rule doubles in weight.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__input:focus-visible,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__select:focus-visible,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__textarea:focus-visible {
    outline: none; border-bottom-color: var(--lead-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 0 var(--lead-accent); background: var(--lead-tint);
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    Chrome paints autofilled fields with its own background, and it lands as a
    square grey slab that covers the underline — the one thing telling the
    visitor this is a field. It is applied by an `!important` UA rule, so
    author `background: transparent` cannot win; there are exactly two levers.
    `background-clip: text` confines that paint to the glyphs themselves, which
    makes it invisible on any transparent field; the 9999s transition delays it
    on engines that ignore the clip. Both are needed, and `:hover` / `:focus`
    are listed because Chrome re-asserts the colour on each.

    Trade-off: while a field is autofilled AND focused, the clip also applies
    to our own focus wash, so focus shows as the 2px accent rule without the
    tint. The rule is the accessible signal; the tint was only ever support.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__input:-webkit-autofill,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__input:-webkit-autofill:hover,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__input:-webkit-autofill:focus,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__input:-webkit-autofill:active,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__textarea:-webkit-autofill,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__textarea:-webkit-autofill:hover,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__textarea:-webkit-autofill:focus {
    -webkit-text-fill-color: currentColor;
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    caret-color: currentColor;
    transition: background-color 9999s ease-out 0s;
  }

  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__select-wrap { position: relative; display: grid; }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__select {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none; cursor: pointer; padding-right: 2rem;
  }
  {%- comment -%} The select was `appearance: none` with nothing put back — a dropdown with no affordance. {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__select-caret {
    position: absolute; right: 0; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 1.15rem; height: 1.15rem; pointer-events: none; opacity: 0.45;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__select-caret svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__select option { background: var(--otodor-black); color: var(--otodor-white); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--light .otodor-lead__select option { background: #fff; color: var(--otodor-ink); }

  {%- comment -%}
    The consent box was the raw UA checkbox — a grey system square against a
    typeset form. Drawn here so it carries the accent and the hairline.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__consent {
    display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; align-items: flex-start; cursor: pointer;
    font-size: var(--otodor-text-sm); line-height: 1.5; opacity: 0.65; margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__consent input {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none; flex: 0 0 auto; margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    width: 1.35rem; height: 1.35rem; border: 1px solid var(--lead-line);
    border-radius: var(--otodor-radius-xs); background: transparent; cursor: pointer;
    display: grid; place-content: center;
    transition: background-color var(--otodor-dur-fast) var(--otodor-ease-out), border-color var(--otodor-dur-fast) var(--otodor-ease-out);
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__consent input::after {
    content: ''; width: 0.35rem; height: 0.65rem; margin-top: -0.15rem;
    border: solid #fff; border-width: 0 2px 2px 0; transform: rotate(45deg) scale(0);
    transition: transform var(--otodor-dur-fast) var(--otodor-ease-spring);
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__consent input:checked { background: var(--lead-accent); border-color: var(--lead-accent); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__consent input:checked::after { transform: rotate(45deg) scale(1); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__consent input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--lead-accent); outline-offset: 2px; }

  /* ─ Actions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
     One filled control on the row. WhatsApp was a saturated green slab
     competing with the primary at equal weight (and carrying a *key* glyph);
     it keeps its full size and the real mark, on a hairline instead of a fill.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__actions {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__submit,
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__wa {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.6rem;
    min-height: var(--otodor-control-h-lg); padding: 0.7rem 1.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--otodor-radius-pill); text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--otodor-text-sm);
    letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-base);
    transition: transform var(--otodor-dur-fast) var(--otodor-ease-out),
                filter var(--otodor-dur-fast) var(--otodor-ease-out),
                border-color var(--otodor-dur-fast) var(--otodor-ease-out);
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__submit {
    flex: 0 1 auto; border: 1px solid var(--lead-accent); cursor: pointer;
    background: var(--lead-accent); color: #fff;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__submit:hover { transform: translateY(var(--otodor-lift-sm)); filter: brightness(1.06); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__submit svg { width: 1.15rem; height: 1.15rem; }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__wa {
    border: 1px solid var(--lead-line); background: transparent; color: inherit;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__wa:hover { border-color: #25D366; transform: translateY(var(--otodor-lift-sm)); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__wa svg { width: 1.3rem; height: 1.3rem; color: #25D366; }
  {%- comment -%}
    Side by side the two pills don't fit a phone, and wrapped they sat at
    their own content widths — 170px over 176px, a ragged left-aligned stack.
    Below the same breakpoint the field row uses, each takes the full width.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__submit,
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__wa { flex: 1 1 100%; }
  }

  /* ─ Success + error states ────────────────────────────────── */
  {%- comment -%}
    The success panel replaces the form in the same column, so it keeps the
    column's left-aligned editorial register rather than becoming a centred
    badge-and-title dialogue.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__success { display: grid; gap: 0.8rem; padding: 0.5rem 0 clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__success-label {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: var(--otodor-text-xs); font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-widest); color: var(--otodor-success);
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__success-label svg { width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem; }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__success-title {
    font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--otodor-text-2xl);
    line-height: var(--otodor-leading-display); letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-tight); margin: 0;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__success-text { margin: 0; font-size: var(--otodor-text-base); line-height: 1.55; opacity: 0.6; max-width: 32rem; }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__errors {
    margin: 0; padding: 0.85rem 0 0.85rem 1rem; border-left: 2px solid #dc2626;
    font-size: var(--otodor-text-sm); line-height: 1.5;
  }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__errors ul { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; opacity: 0.75; }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__field-error { color: #ef5350; font-size: var(--otodor-text-xs); margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}.otodor-lead--light .otodor-lead__field-error { color: #dc2626; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__submit,
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__wa,
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__consent input::after { transition: none; }
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__submit:hover,
    #otodor-lead-{{ section.id }} .otodor-lead__wa:hover { transform: none; }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<section
  id="otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}"
  class="otodor-lead otodor-lead--{{ scheme }}"
  data-otodor-section="lead-form"
  aria-labelledby="otodor-lead-title-{{ section.id }}"
>
  <span id="{{ anchor }}" class="otodor-lead__anchor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <div class="otodor-lead__inner">

    {%- comment -%} ── Left rail: value proposition + trust reasons ── {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="otodor-lead__aside" data-otodor-reveal="fade-up">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <span class="otodor-lead__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="otodor-lead__title" id="otodor-lead-title-{{ section.id }}">
        {{ section.settings.heading | escape }}{% if section.settings.heading_accent != blank %} <span class="accent">{{ section.settings.heading_accent | escape }}</span>{% endif %}
      </h2>
      {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
        <p class="otodor-lead__sub">{{ section.settings.subheading | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if reason_blocks.size > 0 -%}
        <ul class="otodor-lead__reasons" role="list">
          {%- for block in reason_blocks -%}
            <li class="otodor-lead__reason" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- comment -%}
                The index column: a number in the ledger style, the block's own
                glyph in the icon style. Never both — the column is one mark wide.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if section.settings.reason_style == 'icon' and block.settings.icon != blank -%}
                <span class="otodor-lead__reason-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'otodor-icon', name: block.settings.icon %}</span>
              {%- else -%}
                <span class="otodor-lead__reason-index" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              <span>
                {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}<span class="otodor-lead__reason-title">{{ block.settings.title | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}<p class="otodor-lead__reason-text">{{ block.settings.text | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ── Right panel: the native contact form ── {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="otodor-lead__panel" data-otodor-reveal="fade-up">
      {%- form 'contact', id: lead_form_id, class: 'otodor-lead__form' -%}
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <div class="otodor-lead__success" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
            <span class="otodor-lead__success-label">
              <span aria-hidden="true">{% render 'otodor-icon', name: 'warranty' %}</span>
              Confirmed
            </span>
            <h3 class="otodor-lead__success-title">{{ section.settings.success_title | escape }}</h3>
            <p class="otodor-lead__success-text">{{ section.settings.success_text | escape }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
          {%- if form.errors -%}
            <div class="otodor-lead__errors" role="alert" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
              {{ 'templates.contact.form.error_heading' | t }}
              <ul>
                {%- for field in form.errors -%}
                  <li>{{ form.errors.translated_fields[field] | capitalize }} {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}</li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%} Hidden lead-attribution context (arrives as labelled lines in the email). {%- endcomment -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[Source page]" value="{{ canonical_url | escape }}">
          {%- if product != blank -%}<input type="hidden" name="contact[Product]" value="{{ product.title | escape }}">{%- endif -%}
          {%- if collection != blank -%}<input type="hidden" name="contact[Collection]" value="{{ collection.title | escape }}">{%- endif -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[Advisor result]" value="" data-otodor-lead-advisor>

          <div class="otodor-lead__row">
            <div class="otodor-lead__field">
              <label class="otodor-lead__label" for="otodor-lead-name-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.label_name | escape }}</label>
              <input class="otodor-lead__input" type="text" id="otodor-lead-name-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[Name]" autocomplete="name"
                value="{% if form.name %}{{ form.name | escape }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.name | escape }}{% endif %}">
            </div>
            <div class="otodor-lead__field">
              <label class="otodor-lead__label" for="otodor-lead-phone-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.label_phone | escape }} <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
              <input class="otodor-lead__input" type="tel" id="otodor-lead-phone-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[Phone]" autocomplete="tel"
                inputmode="tel" required aria-required="true"
                value="{% if customer %}{{ customer.phone | escape }}{% endif %}">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="otodor-lead__field">
            <label class="otodor-lead__label" for="otodor-lead-email-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.label_email | escape }} <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input class="otodor-lead__input" type="email" id="otodor-lead-email-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[email]"
              autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" aria-required="true"
              {% if form.errors contains 'email' %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="otodor-lead-email-error-{{ section.id }}"{% endif %}
              value="{% if form.email %}{{ form.email | escape }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.email | escape }}{% endif %}">
            {%- if form.errors contains 'email' -%}
              <small class="otodor-lead__field-error" id="otodor-lead-email-error-{{ section.id }}">{{ form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }} {{ form.errors.messages.email }}</small>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          {%- if interest_blocks.size > 0 -%}
            <div class="otodor-lead__field">
              <label class="otodor-lead__label" for="otodor-lead-interest-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.label_interest | escape }}</label>
              <span class="otodor-lead__select-wrap">
                <select class="otodor-lead__select" id="otodor-lead-interest-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[Interest]" data-otodor-lead-interest>
                  <option value="">{{ section.settings.interest_placeholder | escape }}</option>
                  {%- for block in interest_blocks -%}
                    <option value="{{ block.settings.label | escape }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ block.settings.label | escape }}</option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
                <span class="otodor-lead__select-caret" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'otodor-icon', name: 'chevron-down' %}</span>
              </span>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="otodor-lead__field">
            <label class="otodor-lead__label" for="otodor-lead-body-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.label_message | escape }}</label>
            <textarea class="otodor-lead__textarea" id="otodor-lead-body-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[Comment]" data-otodor-lead-message
              placeholder="{{ section.settings.message_placeholder | escape }}">{{ form.body }}</textarea>
          </div>

          {%- if section.settings.show_consent -%}
            <label class="otodor-lead__consent" for="otodor-lead-consent-{{ section.id }}">
              <input type="checkbox" id="otodor-lead-consent-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[Consent]" value="Yes"
                {% if section.settings.consent_required %}required aria-required="true"{% endif %}>
              <span>{{ section.settings.consent_text | escape }}</span>
            </label>
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="otodor-lead__actions">
            <button type="submit" class="otodor-lead__submit">
              {{ section.settings.submit_label | escape }}
              <span aria-hidden="true">{% render 'otodor-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}</span>
            </button>
            {%- if wa_enabled -%}
              <a class="otodor-lead__wa" href="{{ wa_link }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                aria-label="{{ section.settings.whatsapp_label | escape }} (opens WhatsApp)"
                data-otodor-lead-wa
                data-wa-number="{{ wa_number | escape }}"
                data-wa-intro="{{ wa_intro | escape }}"
                data-l-name="{{ section.settings.label_name | escape }}"
                data-l-phone="{{ section.settings.label_phone | escape }}"
                data-l-email="{{ section.settings.label_email | escape }}"
                data-l-interest="{{ section.settings.label_interest | escape }}"
                data-l-message="{{ section.settings.label_message | escape }}">
                <span aria-hidden="true">{% render 'otodor-icon', name: 'whatsapp' %}</span>
                {{ section.settings.whatsapp_label | escape }}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  Advisor / CTA handoff: prefill interest + message from ?interest= / ?product= / ?msg= query params
  (used by otodor-advisor and any deep-linked "Get a quote" CTA). Progressive enhancement only.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('otodor-lead-{{ section.id }}');
    if (!root) return;
    var params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
    var interest = params.get('interest');
    var product = params.get('product');
    var msg = params.get('msg');

    var sel = root.querySelector('[data-otodor-lead-interest]');
    if (interest && sel) {
      var matched = false;
      Array.prototype.forEach.call(sel.options, function (opt) {
        if (opt.value.toLowerCase() === interest.toLowerCase()) { opt.selected = true; matched = true; }
      });
      if (!matched) {
        var o = document.createElement('option');
        o.value = interest; o.textContent = interest; o.selected = true;
        sel.appendChild(o);
      }
    }
    var adv = root.querySelector('[data-otodor-lead-advisor]');
    if (adv && (interest || product)) adv.value = product || interest;

    var body = root.querySelector('[data-otodor-lead-message]');
    if (body && msg && !body.value.trim()) body.value = msg;

    // ── Dynamic WhatsApp message: fold in whatever the visitor has typed ──
    var wa = root.querySelector('[data-otodor-lead-wa]');
    if (wa) {
      var num = wa.getAttribute('data-wa-number');
      var intro = wa.getAttribute('data-wa-intro') || '';
      var fields = [
        ['data-l-name', 'contact[Name]'],
        ['data-l-phone', 'contact[Phone]'],
        ['data-l-email', 'contact[email]'],
        ['data-l-interest', 'contact[Interest]'],
        ['data-l-message', 'contact[Comment]']
      ];
      var stripStar = function (s) { return (s || '').replace(/\s*\*+\s*$/, '').trim(); };
      var valOf = function (name) {
        var el = root.querySelector('[name="' + name + '"]');
        return el && el.value ? el.value.trim() : '';
      };
      var rebuildWa = function () {
        var lines = [];
        if (intro) lines.push(intro);
        fields.forEach(function (f) {
          var v = valOf(f[1]);
          if (v) lines.push(stripStar(wa.getAttribute(f[0])) + ': ' + v);
        });
        wa.setAttribute('href', 'https://wa.me/' + num + '?text=' + encodeURIComponent(lines.join('\n')));
      };
      root.addEventListener('input', rebuildWa);
      root.addEventListener('change', rebuildWa);
      rebuildWa();
    }
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "OTODOR Lead Form",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "shopify-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Native quote / consultation capture. Submissions arrive at your store's contact email (Settings → Notifications). Hidden fields auto-attach which product / collection / page the lead came from." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "anchor_id", "label": "Anchor id (for CTA deep-links)", "default": "otodor-lead", "info": "Link CTAs to this page with #otodor-lead to scroll straight to the form." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Colour scheme", "options": [ { "value": "light", "label": "Light" }, { "value": "dark", "label": "Dark" } ], "default": "light" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "form_first", "label": "Show form first on mobile", "default": false },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Value proposition (left rail)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Talk to a specialist" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Request a" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading_accent", "label": "Heading accent (coloured)", "default": "custom quote." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "subheading", "label": "Subheading", "default": "Tell us about your door and we'll recommend the right OTODOR system, with a free site survey and installation assessment." },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "reason_style", "label": "Trust reason style", "default": "ledger",
      "info": "Ledger = hairline-ruled rows with a numbered index (recommended). Icon = the block's glyph instead of the number.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "ledger", "label": "Ledger (numbered rows)" },
        { "value": "icon", "label": "Icon" }
      ]
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Form labels" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_name", "label": "Name label", "default": "Name" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_phone", "label": "Phone label", "default": "Phone" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_email", "label": "Email label", "default": "Email" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_interest", "label": "Interest label", "default": "What are you looking for?" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "interest_placeholder", "label": "Interest placeholder", "default": "Select a category" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_message", "label": "Message label", "default": "Tell us more (optional)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "message_placeholder", "label": "Message placeholder", "default": "Door type, address area, timeline…" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "submit_label", "label": "Submit button label", "default": "Request my quote" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Consent" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_consent", "label": "Show consent checkbox", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "consent_required", "label": "Consent is required", "default": false },
    { "type": "text", "id": "consent_text", "label": "Consent text", "default": "I agree to be contacted by OTODOR about my enquiry." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "WhatsApp (instant path)" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_whatsapp", "label": "Show WhatsApp button", "default": true, "info": "Uses the store WhatsApp number (Theme settings → OTODOR WhatsApp Settings)." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "whatsapp_label", "label": "WhatsApp button label", "default": "Chat on WhatsApp" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "whatsapp_message", "label": "WhatsApp pre-filled message", "default": "Hello OTODOR, I'd like a quote for a smart lock." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Success message" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "success_title", "label": "Success title", "default": "Request received." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "success_text", "label": "Success text", "default": "Thank you — an OTODOR specialist will call you within one business day to arrange your survey." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Spacing" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_top", "label": "Top padding", "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 80 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_bottom", "label": "Bottom padding", "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 80 }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "reason",
      "name": "Trust reason",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon", "default": "warranty",
          "options": [
            { "value": "", "label": "None" },
            { "value": "warranty", "label": "Warranty / Shield" },
            { "value": "fingerprint", "label": "Fingerprint" },
            { "value": "installation", "label": "Installation" },
            { "value": "smart", "label": "Smart / Support" },
            { "value": "remote", "label": "Remote" },
            { "value": "star", "label": "Star" }
          ]
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "3-year warranty" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Text", "default": "Every OTODOR lock is covered for three years." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "interest",
      "name": "Interest option",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Option label", "default": "Wooden door lock" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "OTODOR Lead Form",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "reason", "settings": { "icon": "warranty", "title": "3-year warranty", "text": "Every OTODOR lock is covered for three years." } },
        { "type": "reason", "settings": { "icon": "installation", "title": "Free site survey", "text": "A specialist assesses your door before you buy." } },
        { "type": "reason", "settings": { "icon": "smart", "title": "16 years' heritage", "text": "Backed by NavKar's security engineering track record." } },
        { "type": "interest", "settings": { "label": "Wooden door lock" } },
        { "type": "interest", "settings": { "label": "Glass door lock" } },
        { "type": "interest", "settings": { "label": "Metal gate lock" } },
        { "type": "interest", "settings": { "label": "Smart padlock" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
